-- title:
--   Honda system of a unipotent k-vector space scheme over ℤₚ
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a finite field $k$ of characteristic $p$, together with a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra structure on $\mathbb{Z}/p$ whose structure map has kernel the ideal generated by $p$. Let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying a cocommutative Hopf algebra structure over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ which is finite and free as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-module, and assume that [`CartierDual (ZMod p) ((ZMod p) ⊗[ℤ_[p]] H)`](def/HopfAlgebra_CartierDual.html#L12), i.e. the $(\mathbb{Z}/p)$-linear dual of the base change $(\mathbb{Z}/p)\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}H$ with its convolution ring structure, is a local ring. Let $n$ be a natural number with $\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb{Z}_p}H=(\#k)^n$, and let $\theta$ assign to each $a\in k$ a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-bialgebra endomorphism $\theta(a)$ of $H$, such that $\theta(ab)=\theta(a)\circ\theta(b)$, $\theta(1)=\mathrm{id}$, and, for the convolution monoid structure on algebra endomorphisms of $H$, $\theta(a+b)=\theta(a)*\theta(b)$ and $\theta(0)$ is the convolution unit. The conclusion asserts the existence of a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space $D$, a Honda system $\mathcal{H}$ over $k$ with parameter $0$ on $D$ — that is, $k$-linear maps $F,V:D\to D$ with $F\circ V=V\circ F=0$ and a $k$-submodule $L\subseteq D$ satisfying: every $x\in L$ lying in the range of $F$ equals $0\cdot y$ for some $y\in L$, for $y\in L$ one has $0\cdot y$ in the range of $F$, $\operatorname{range}F+L=D$, and $V$ is injective on $L$ — and an isomorphism of additive groups $\iota$ from $D$ onto the Dieudonné module `Deundonne`-style direct limit [`Deformation.DieudonneModule (ZMod p) p ((ZMod p) ⊗[ℤ_[p]] H)`](def/Dieudonne_WittHomColimit.html#L234), the colimit over $m$ of the groups of truncated Witt vectors of length $m$ over $(\mathbb{Z}/p)\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}H$ satisfying the homomorphism condition for the comultiplication, such that $\iota$ carries $\mathcal{H}.F$ to `frobenius`, $\mathcal{H}.V$ to `verschiebung`, identifies $\mathcal{H}.L$ with the preimage of the Fontaine submodule [`Deformation.fontaineHodge`](def/Dieudonne_FontaineHodge.html#L272) attached to the ring map underlying $\mathrm{includeRight}:H\to(\mathbb{Z}/p)\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_p}H$ (the classes of elements whose underlying truncated Witt vector lies in `fontaineKer` for that map), and transports multiplication by $a\in k$ into the functorial map on Dieudonné modules induced by $\mathrm{id}\otimes\theta(a)$; finally $\dim_k D=n$.
--
--   This is Fontaine's classification of unipotent finite flat commutative group schemes over $\mathbb{Z}_p$ by finite Honda systems, in the form adapted to a $k$-vector space scheme structure: the $k$-action coming from $\theta$ makes the Dieudonné module of the special fibre a Honda system over $k$ of dimension $n$. It is used in the construction of Fontaine–Conrad presentations for residual Galois representations and in the bound on the endomorphisms of the resulting Honda system.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Deformation_DieudonneModule_exists_hondaSystem_addEquiv_smul_eq_map_of_isLocalRing_cartierDual.lean

